## AppShell state (src/core/shell/AppShell.tsx)
- Reads gameId, gameName, gameType from localStorage
- `normalizeGameType()` in `src/core/gameTypeMap.ts` normalizes type strings to canonical uppercase game ids
- All game routing goes through AppShell — don't create standalone game routes

## ThemeProvider (src/core/theme/ — barrel `index.ts`, implementation `theme.tsx`)
- Wraps game screens with CSS variables from GameDefinition.colors
- Use `var(--game-primary)` and `var(--game-accent)` in game component styles
- Don't hardcode colors inside game components — use CSS vars

## Orientation layout
- Games can specify landscape/portrait preference
- AppShell handles orientation prompts — don't add your own rotation logic

## Mandatory GameScreen layout reuse
- For new games, always reuse `src/core/ui/gameScreenLayout.ts` tokens.
- Landscape must use `GAME_LANDSCAPE_THREE_COL_GRID` and `GAME_LANDSCAPE_CENTER_CARD`.
- Landscape left column must use `GameLandscapeInfoColumn` (logo + instructions + QR/context).
- Landscape right column must render `sidebarElement` from `GameScreenProps`; do not reimplement shell widgets.
- Portrait must include `GAME_PORTRAIT_QR_INSTRUCTIONS_GRID` for QR + instructions.
- Avoid ad-hoc/custom layout grids when shared layout components/tokens already exist.
